{"id":91,"agencyId":717,"allowEmailAlert":false,"emailAlertsCases":false,"emailAlertsIncidents":false,"emailAlertsMostWanted":false,"emailAlertsMissingPersons":false,"emailAlertsStolenVehicles":false,"welcomeMessage":"<p><span style=\"background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); font-size: 11pt; font-family: &quot;Calibri Light&quot;, sans-serif; color: inherit;\">The City of Redwood City provides this police data for reference purposes only. The information is not intended to be used for legal, investigative, or other official purposes.\u00A0The information displayed is sourced from our Records Management System and reflects cases managed by the Redwood City Police Department. To safeguard the privacy of victims, this site does not include information about juvenile offenders or certain sensitive calls for service.\u00A0The City makes reasonable efforts to produce and publish accurate information, and the data is updated on a regular, automated basis. However, the City makes no warranty, expressed or implied, representation, or guarantee as to the content, sequence, accuracy, timeliness, or completeness of the data provided. This information is provided “as is,” and the City expressly disclaims all warranties, including, without limitation, the implied warranties of merchantability and fitness for a particular purpose.</span></p><p><span style=\"background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); font-size: 11pt; font-family: &quot;Calibri Light&quot;, sans-serif; color: inherit;\">The City assumes no liability for any errors, omissions, or inaccuracies in the information provided, regardless of cause. The City also assumes no liability for any decisions made or actions taken or not taken by users in reliance upon any information or data provided through this site.</span></p><p><span style=\"background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); font-size: 11pt; font-family: &quot;Calibri Light&quot;, sans-serif; color: inherit;\">Use of this site indicates your unconditional acceptance of this disclaimer.</span></p>","aboutPageUrl":"https://www.redwoodcity.org/departments/police-department/report-crime-online","showOnMainMap":true,"showExploreAnotherAgency":true,"defaultMapType":"Physical","enableStreetView":false,"defaultLatitude":37.49333,"defaultLongitude":-122.220764,"locationHintText":"1301 Maple St, Redwood City, CA","locationDefaultCity":"Redwood City, CA","enableMapCluster":false,"incidentsEnabled":true,"liveIncidentsEnabled":false,"caseDataEnabled":true,"onlyApprovedCases":true,"bulletinEnabled":false,"keepHistoricalBulletins":false,"mostWantedEnabled":false,"missingPersonsEnabled":false,"stolenVehiclesEnabled":true,"stolenVehiclesText":"<p><span style=\"background-color: rgb(236, 237, 243); font-size: 16px; font-family: PublicSans, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; color: rgb(73, 81, 99);\">Disclaimer: The information provided on this page regarding stolen vehicles is compiled and maintained by the Redwood City Police Department. While we strive to ensure the accuracy and timeliness of the information presented, we cannot guarantee that all details are current, complete, or free from error. This information is provided for general awareness and should not be relied upon as official documentation. Please do not take direct action if you see any of the stolen vehicles listed, call the Redwood City Police Department at 650-780-7118.</span></p>","warrantsEnabled":false,"warrantPhotosEnabled":false,"arrestsEnabled":true,"arrestPhotosEnabled":false,"arrestsShowName":false,"arrestsShowDateOfBirth":false,"arrestsShowAge":true,"arrestsShowSex":true,"arrestsShowRace":true,"arrestsShowHeight":false,"arrestsShowWeight":false,"arrestsShowHairColor":false,"arrestsShowEyeColor":false,"arrestsShowOccupation":false,"arrestsShowLocation":true,"arrestsShowActionTaken":true,"arrestsShowIncidentNumber":false,"arrestsShowCaseNumber":true,"arrestsShowCharges":true,"arrestsEnabledForUnapprovedCases":false,"arrestAgeOut":30,"arrestExcludeCharges":"","arrestText":"<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><br></p><p><span style=\"background-color: rgb(236, 237, 243); font-size: 16px; font-family: PublicSans, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; color: rgb(73, 81, 99);\">Using this website, members of the public will have access to public information regarding individuals arrested by the Redwood City Police Department. The information is on a rolling 30-day basis, after 30 days the information is considered criminal history and no longer releasable to the public. Be advised that during the course of any investigation any offense charges can be changed or updated. Unless otherwise declared &quot;guilty&quot; or &quot;convicted,&quot; offenders are considered innocent until proven guilty in a court of law.</span></p>","inmatesEnabled":false,"inmatesPhotosEnabled":false,"inmatesShowName":false,"inmatesShowDateOfBirth":false,"inmatesShowAge":false,"inmatesShowSex":false,"inmatesShowRace":false,"inmatesShowHeight":false,"inmatesShowWeight":false,"inmatesShowHairColor":false,"inmatesShowEyeColor":false,"inmatesShowBuild":false,"inmatesShowComplexion":false,"inmatesShowInmateRealAddress":false,"inmatesRequireBookingComplete":false,"inmatesRequireBookingWithArrestLocation":false,"inmatesRequireBookingWithArrestAgency":false,"inmatesConvertToReleaseAgeOut":false,"crimeStatsEnabled":true,"pressReleaseEnabled":false,"dailyCrimeFireLogEnabled":false,"dailyCrimeFireLogDaysIncluded":0,"dailyCrimeFireLogDaysDelay":0,"dailyCrimeFireLogShowNoRecord":false,"vacationCheckEnabled":false,"vacationCheckPreferredTimes":true,"vacationCheckRequestedChecksPerDay":true,"directedPatrolEnabled":false,"directedPatrolPreferredTimes":true,"directedPatrolRequestedChecksPerDay":true,"securityCameraEnabled":true,"securityCameraDisclaimer":"<p><span style=\"background-color: rgb(250, 250, 250); font-size: 16px; font-family: PublicSans, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.87);\">The Redwood City Police Department&#39;s Surveillance Camera Registry enables residents and business owners to voluntarily register their surveillance cameras with the department. While the Police Department will not have direct access to the camera systems, registration allows officers to identify the presence of cameras in the vicinity when investigating crimes in or around the neighborhood.</span></p>","securityCameraAdditionalInfoInstructions":"<p>Please be specific in the additional information field. Describe where the cameras are located and what is captured. This will save us and you time if we are investigating a crime in your neighborhood. </p><p>Example: outdoor camera over driveway views sidewalk and parts of Main St. </p>","securityCameraSuccessText":"<p>Your security camera registration request was successfully submitted to the Redwood City Police Department. </p>","securityCameraEmailAlerts":"brichardson@redwoodcity.org","agencySiteName":"Redwood City Police Department","enableMapFeatures":false,"showPlace":false,"crimeStatsDisclaimer":"<p><span style=\"background-color: rgb(236, 237, 243); font-size: 16px; font-family: PublicSans, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; color: rgb(73, 81, 99);\">Crime statistics serve as an essential tool for comprehensively analyzing, interpreting, and responding to patterns of criminal activity within a society. The data presented in this report is dynamic and subject to ongoing revisions, as it is continuously sourced from the Police Department&#39;s Records Management System (RIMS) and updated on a daily basis.</span></p>","crimeStatsChartType":"Bar","stopDataStatsEnabled":true,"stopDataStatsDisclaimer":"<p><span style=\"background-color: rgb(236, 237, 243); font-size: 16px; font-family: PublicSans, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; color: rgb(73, 81, 99);\">Demographic information is recorded solely based on the officer&#39;s direct observation and initial perception at the time of the stop. It is not gathered through direct inquiry, nor is it derived from the individual&#39;s driver&#39;s license or other forms of identification. As a result, the reported demographic details may not correspond with the individual&#39;s official documentation or self-identified characteristics.</span></p>","stopDataStatsDefinitions":"<ul><li><span style=\"color: rgb(73, 81, 99); font-family: PublicSans, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; font-size: 13px; background-color: rgb(236, 237, 243);\">“</span><strong style=\"color: rgb(73, 81, 99); font-family: PublicSans, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; font-size: 13px; background-color: rgb(236, 237, 243);\">Reason for Stop</strong><span style=\"color: rgb(73, 81, 99); font-family: PublicSans, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; font-size: 13px; background-color: rgb(236, 237, 243);\">” refers to the primary reason why the officer stopped the person.</span><ul><li><span style=\"background-color: rgb(236, 237, 243); font-size: 13px; font-family: PublicSans, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; color: rgb(73, 81, 99);\">Traffic violation</span></li><li><span style=\"background-color: rgb(236, 237, 243); font-size: 13px; font-family: PublicSans, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; color: rgb(73, 81, 99);\">Reasonable suspicion that the person was engaged in criminal activity</span></li><li><span style=\"background-color: rgb(236, 237, 243); font-size: 13px; font-family: PublicSans, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; color: rgb(73, 81, 99);\">Probable cause to arrest or search</span></li><li><span style=\"background-color: rgb(236, 237, 243); font-size: 13px; font-family: PublicSans, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; color: rgb(73, 81, 99);\">Probable cause to take into custody under Welfare and Institutions Code section 5150</span></li><li><span style=\"background-color: rgb(236, 237, 243); font-size: 13px; font-family: PublicSans, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; color: rgb(73, 81, 99);\">Known to be on parole/probation/PRCS/mandatory supervision</span></li><li><span style=\"background-color: rgb(236, 237, 243); font-size: 13px; font-family: PublicSans, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; color: rgb(73, 81, 99);\">Knowledge of outstanding arrest warrant/wanted person</span></li><li><span style=\"background-color: rgb(236, 237, 243); font-size: 13px; font-family: PublicSans, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; color: rgb(73, 81, 99);\">Investigation to determine whether the person is truant</span></li><li><span style=\"background-color: rgb(236, 237, 243); font-size: 13px; font-family: PublicSans, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; color: rgb(73, 81, 99);\">Consensual encounter resulting in a search</span></li></ul></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(73, 81, 99); font-family: PublicSans, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; font-size: 13px; background-color: rgb(236, 237, 243);\">“</span><strong style=\"color: rgb(73, 81, 99); font-family: PublicSans, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; font-size: 13px; background-color: rgb(236, 237, 243);\">Perceived Race or Ethnicity of Person Stopped</strong><span style=\"color: rgb(73, 81, 99); font-family: PublicSans, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; font-size: 13px; background-color: rgb(236, 237, 243);\">” refers to the officer’s perception of the race or ethnicity of the person stopped. When reporting this data element, the officer shall make their determination of the person’s race or ethnicity based on personal observation only. The officer shall not ask the person stopped their race or ethnicity, or ask questions or make comments or statements designed to elicit this information. Officers may report one or more of the following options for the person stopped:</span><ul><li><span style=\"background-color: rgb(236, 237, 243); font-size: 13px; font-family: PublicSans, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; color: rgb(73, 81, 99);\">Asian</span></li><li><span style=\"background-color: rgb(236, 237, 243); font-size: 13px; font-family: PublicSans, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; color: rgb(73, 81, 99);\">Black/African American</span></li><li><span style=\"background-color: rgb(236, 237, 243); font-size: 13px; font-family: PublicSans, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; color: rgb(73, 81, 99);\">Hispanic/Latine(x)</span></li><li><span style=\"background-color: rgb(236, 237, 243); font-size: 13px; font-family: PublicSans, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; color: rgb(73, 81, 99);\">Middle Eastern or South Asian</span></li><li><span style=\"background-color: rgb(236, 237, 243); font-size: 13px; font-family: PublicSans, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; color: rgb(73, 81, 99);\">Native American</span></li><li><span style=\"background-color: rgb(236, 237, 243); font-size: 13px; font-family: PublicSans, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; color: rgb(73, 81, 99);\">Pacific Islander</span></li><li><span style=\"background-color: rgb(236, 237, 243); font-size: 13px; font-family: PublicSans, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; color: rgb(73, 81, 99);\">White</span></li></ul></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(73, 81, 99); font-family: PublicSans, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; font-size: 13px; background-color: rgb(236, 237, 243);\">“</span><strong style=\"color: rgb(73, 81, 99); font-family: PublicSans, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; font-size: 13px; background-color: rgb(236, 237, 243);\">Perceived Gender of Person Stopped</strong><span style=\"color: rgb(73, 81, 99); font-family: PublicSans, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; font-size: 13px; background-color: rgb(236, 237, 243);\">” refers to the officer’s perception of the person’s gender. When reporting this data element, the officer shall make their determination of the person’s gender based on personal observation only. The officer shall not ask the person stopped their gender or use the gender specified on the person’s driver’s license or other identification, recognizing that the officer’s observation may not reflect the gender specified on the person’s identification</span><ul><li><span style=\"background-color: rgb(236, 237, 243); font-size: 13px; font-family: PublicSans, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; color: rgb(73, 81, 99);\">Cisgender man/boy</span></li><li><span style=\"background-color: rgb(236, 237, 243); font-size: 13px; font-family: PublicSans, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; color: rgb(73, 81, 99);\">Cisgender woman/girl</span></li><li><span style=\"background-color: rgb(236, 237, 243); font-size: 13px; font-family: PublicSans, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; color: rgb(73, 81, 99);\">Transgender man/boy</span></li><li><span style=\"background-color: rgb(236, 237, 243); font-size: 13px; font-family: PublicSans, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; color: rgb(73, 81, 99);\">Transgender woman/girl</span></li><li><span style=\"background-color: rgb(236, 237, 243); font-size: 13px; font-family: PublicSans, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; color: rgb(73, 81, 99);\">Nonbinary person</span></li></ul></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(73, 81, 99); font-family: PublicSans, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; font-size: 13px; background-color: rgb(236, 237, 243);\">“</span><strong style=\"color: rgb(73, 81, 99); font-family: PublicSans, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; font-size: 13px; background-color: rgb(236, 237, 243);\">Perceived or Known Disability of Person Stopped</strong><span style=\"color: rgb(73, 81, 99); font-family: PublicSans, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; font-size: 13px; background-color: rgb(236, 237, 243);\">” refers to the officer’s perception that the person stopped displayed signs of one or more of the following conditions; the officer’s knowledge that the person stopped has one or more of the following conditions because the person stopped so advised the officer; or the officer’s prior knowledge that the person stopped had one or more of the following conditions.</span><ul><li><span style=\"background-color: rgb(236, 237, 243); font-size: 13px; font-family: PublicSans, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; color: rgb(73, 81, 99);\">Deafness or difficulty hearing</span></li><li><span style=\"background-color: rgb(236, 237, 243); font-size: 13px; font-family: PublicSans, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; color: rgb(73, 81, 99);\">Speech impairment or limited use of language</span></li><li><span style=\"background-color: rgb(236, 237, 243); font-size: 13px; font-family: PublicSans, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; color: rgb(73, 81, 99);\">Blind or limited vision</span></li><li><span style=\"background-color: rgb(236, 237, 243); font-size: 13px; font-family: PublicSans, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; color: rgb(73, 81, 99);\">Mental health condition</span></li><li><span style=\"background-color: rgb(236, 237, 243); font-size: 13px; font-family: PublicSans, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; color: rgb(73, 81, 99);\">Intellectual or developmental disability, including dementia</span></li><li><span style=\"background-color: rgb(236, 237, 243); font-size: 13px; font-family: PublicSans, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; color: rgb(73, 81, 99);\">Other disability</span></li><li><span style=\"background-color: rgb(236, 237, 243); font-size: 13px; font-family: PublicSans, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; color: rgb(73, 81, 99);\">None</span></li></ul></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(73, 81, 99); font-family: PublicSans, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; font-size: 13px; background-color: rgb(236, 237, 243);\">&quot;</span><strong style=\"color: rgb(73, 81, 99); font-family: PublicSans, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; font-size: 13px; background-color: rgb(236, 237, 243);\">Actions Taken During Stop</strong><span style=\"color: rgb(73, 81, 99); font-family: PublicSans, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; font-size: 13px; background-color: rgb(236, 237, 243);\">&quot; refers to (more than one can be selected)</span><ul><li><span style=\"background-color: rgb(236, 237, 243); font-size: 13px; font-family: PublicSans, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; color: rgb(73, 81, 99);\">Asked for consent to search person</span></li><li><span style=\"background-color: rgb(236, 237, 243); font-size: 13px; font-family: PublicSans, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; color: rgb(73, 81, 99);\">Asked for consent to search property</span></li><li><span style=\"background-color: rgb(236, 237, 243); font-size: 13px; font-family: PublicSans, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; color: rgb(73, 81, 99);\">Asked for identification of stopped persons passenger</span></li><li><span style=\"background-color: rgb(236, 237, 243); font-size: 13px; font-family: PublicSans, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; color: rgb(73, 81, 99);\">Asked whether the person is on parole, probations, PRCS, or some other form of mandatory supervision</span></li><li><span style=\"background-color: rgb(236, 237, 243); font-size: 13px; font-family: PublicSans, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; color: rgb(73, 81, 99);\">Canine used to search for, locate, and/or detect contraband</span></li><li><span style=\"background-color: rgb(236, 237, 243); font-size: 13px; font-family: PublicSans, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; color: rgb(73, 81, 99);\">Curbside detention</span></li><li><span style=\"background-color: rgb(236, 237, 243); font-size: 13px; font-family: PublicSans, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; color: rgb(73, 81, 99);\">Field sobriety test conducted</span></li><li><span style=\"background-color: rgb(236, 237, 243); font-size: 13px; font-family: PublicSans, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; color: rgb(73, 81, 99);\">Frisk/past search of the persons outer clothing was conducted</span></li><li><span style=\"background-color: rgb(236, 237, 243); font-size: 13px; font-family: PublicSans, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; color: rgb(73, 81, 99);\">None</span></li><li><span style=\"background-color: rgb(236, 237, 243); font-size: 13px; font-family: PublicSans, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; color: rgb(73, 81, 99);\">Patrol car detention</span></li><li><span style=\"background-color: rgb(236, 237, 243); font-size: 13px; font-family: PublicSans, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; color: rgb(73, 81, 99);\">Person photographed</span></li><li><span style=\"background-color: rgb(236, 237, 243); font-size: 13px; font-family: PublicSans, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; color: rgb(73, 81, 99);\">Person removed from vehicle by order</span></li><li><span style=\"background-color: rgb(236, 237, 243); font-size: 13px; font-family: PublicSans, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; color: rgb(73, 81, 99);\">Property was seized</span></li><li><span style=\"background-color: rgb(236, 237, 243); font-size: 13px; font-family: PublicSans, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; color: rgb(73, 81, 99);\">Ran name of stopped persons passenger</span></li><li><span style=\"background-color: rgb(236, 237, 243); font-size: 13px; font-family: PublicSans, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; color: rgb(73, 81, 99);\">Search of person was conducted</span></li><li><span style=\"background-color: rgb(236, 237, 243); font-size: 13px; font-family: PublicSans, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; color: rgb(73, 81, 99);\">Search of property was conducted</span></li><li><span style=\"background-color: rgb(236, 237, 243); font-size: 13px; font-family: PublicSans, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; color: rgb(73, 81, 99);\">Vehicle impounded</span></li><li><span style=\"background-color: rgb(236, 237, 243); font-size: 13px; font-family: PublicSans, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; color: rgb(73, 81, 99);\">Baton or other impact weapon drawn</span></li><li><span style=\"background-color: rgb(236, 237, 243); font-size: 13px; font-family: PublicSans, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; color: rgb(73, 81, 99);\">Baton or other impact weapon used</span></li><li><span style=\"background-color: rgb(236, 237, 243); font-size: 13px; font-family: PublicSans, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; color: rgb(73, 81, 99);\">Chemical spray used</span></li><li><span style=\"background-color: rgb(236, 237, 243); font-size: 13px; font-family: PublicSans, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; color: rgb(73, 81, 99);\">Electronic control device pointed at person or sparked</span></li><li><span style=\"background-color: rgb(236, 237, 243); font-size: 13px; font-family: PublicSans, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; color: rgb(73, 81, 99);\">Electronic control device used in dart-mode</span></li><li><span style=\"background-color: rgb(236, 237, 243); font-size: 13px; font-family: PublicSans, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; color: rgb(73, 81, 99);\">Electronic control device used in drive-stun mode</span></li><li><span style=\"background-color: rgb(236, 237, 243); font-size: 13px; font-family: PublicSans, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; color: rgb(73, 81, 99);\">Firearm discharged</span></li><li><span style=\"background-color: rgb(236, 237, 243); font-size: 13px; font-family: PublicSans, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; color: rgb(73, 81, 99);\">Firearm pointed as person</span></li><li><span style=\"background-color: rgb(236, 237, 243); font-size: 13px; font-family: PublicSans, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; color: rgb(73, 81, 99);\">Firearm unholstered</span></li><li><span style=\"background-color: rgb(236, 237, 243); font-size: 13px; font-family: PublicSans, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; color: rgb(73, 81, 99);\">Handcuffed or flex cuffed</span></li><li><span style=\"background-color: rgb(236, 237, 243); font-size: 13px; font-family: PublicSans, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; color: rgb(73, 81, 99);\">Impact projectile discharged or used</span></li><li><span style=\"background-color: rgb(236, 237, 243); font-size: 13px; font-family: PublicSans, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; color: rgb(73, 81, 99);\">Impact projectile weapon pointed as person</span></li><li><span style=\"background-color: rgb(236, 237, 243); font-size: 13px; font-family: PublicSans, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; color: rgb(73, 81, 99);\">Officer&#39;s canine bit or held person</span></li><li><span style=\"background-color: rgb(236, 237, 243); font-size: 13px; font-family: PublicSans, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; color: rgb(73, 81, 99);\">Officer&#39;s canine removed from vehicle or used to search</span></li><li><span style=\"background-color: rgb(236, 237, 243); font-size: 13px; font-family: PublicSans, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; color: rgb(73, 81, 99);\">Person removed from vehicle by physical contact</span></li><li><span style=\"background-color: rgb(236, 237, 243); font-size: 13px; font-family: PublicSans, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; color: rgb(73, 81, 99);\">Physical compliance tactics and techniques</span></li><li><span style=\"background-color: rgb(236, 237, 243); font-size: 13px; font-family: PublicSans, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; color: rgb(73, 81, 99);\">Use of vehicle in apprehension of stopped person</span></li></ul></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(73, 81, 99); font-family: PublicSans, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; font-size: 13px; background-color: rgb(236, 237, 243);\">&quot;</span><strong style=\"color: rgb(73, 81, 99); font-family: PublicSans, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; font-size: 13px; background-color: rgb(236, 237, 243);\">Search Rates</strong><span style=\"color: rgb(73, 81, 99); font-family: PublicSans, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; font-size: 13px; background-color: rgb(236, 237, 243);\">&quot; refers to stops with actions “Search of person was conducted” and “Search of property was conducted” for each perceived gender</span></li><li>&quot;<strong style=\"color: rgb(73, 81, 99); font-family: PublicSans, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-